<title>ABU DHABI: United Arab Emirates 1995 real GDP rises 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>United Arab Emirates 1995 real GDP rises 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Arab Emirates real gross domestic product (GDP) rose 2.1 percent in 1995 compared to a 1.9-percent fall in 1994, Ministry of Planning figures show.</p>
<p>Percentage change over one year:</p>
<p>							1995	    1994</p>
<p> Real GDP (1985 prices)			 +2.1	    -1.9</p>
<p> GDP at current prices			  +6.6	    +2.2</p>
<p>GDP in millions of UAE dirhams over one year:</p>
<p>							1995	    1994</p>
<p> Real GDP  (1985 prices)		   102,106	 100,050</p>
<p> GDP at current prices		     143,970	 135,068</p>
<p>Contribution to real GDP by sectors in millions of dirhams</p>
<p>								1995</p>
<p> Agriculture, livestock and fishing		2,518</p>
<p> Crude oil						34,894</p>
<p> Other mining and quarrying industries	     319</p>
<p> Manufacturing					   8,865</p>
<p> Electricity and water				 2,277</p>
<p> Construction					    9,433</p>
<p> Hotels and maintenance services		  12,624</p>
<p> Transport, storage and communication	    6,028</p>
<p> Finance and insurance				 5,071</p>
<p> Real estate and business services		 8,298</p>
<p> Other services					  1,163</p>
<p> LESS: Imputed bank services			(1,808)</p>
<p> Government services				  11,574</p>
<p> Domestic services and households		    851</p>
</text>
